e profile's literal epoch 12 is thereby machine-checked); the M arms are bound through the profile's pinned sha256 as before. (A7, 2026-09-12 23:5x, from the Fable round-3 review, finding 4) §5's generic "Cohorts (registered)" bullet is read as: a plotted curve point and its seed SD use the arm's own cohort (queries finite for all five seeds of that arm and metric); a comparison cell — including the fixed target of an H2 cell — uses the paired cohort (queries finite for all five seeds in both arms of the cell), the baseline's own-cohort mean being shown separately and labelled with both cohort sizes; this is the amended H2 rule the producer implements. (A8, same time, finding 1) The tier curve's single-delta contract is machine-checked: the producer admits an S/L run only with `train_manifest` and `train_completion` bound, requires the four new arms' training-launcher closure digests to equal each other and the approved `closures.training_launcher` pin, and checks the full §3 recipe keys (`num_shot, max_len, lr, weight_decay, decay_epochs, lr_gamma, epochs, batch_size, accum_steps, seed, tf32`) of the bound `args.json`. (A9, 2026-09-14 14:4x, from the Fable round-4 review, item 5) The approval record's `closures.training_launcher` is a LIST of approved training-launcher closure digests — `0bff0d4f…` (launch commit `f19b9b6`: S_simple, S_cylindrical, L_cylindrical) and `efde5a31…` (commit `f7b10b5`, round 4: receipt/arm binding and preflight ordering only; L_simple) — each reviewed; the producer requires every new arm's recorded launcher digest to be in the list and, as the single-delta check proper, the four arms' TRAINING closure digests (trainer + its imports, unchanged since `f19b9b6`) to be equal to each other and to the approved `closures.training` pin, and the §3 recipe dict to match type-strictly.

